//! `std::hint`: hints to the compiler (docs/adr/0090-benchmarks.md, Q596).
//!
//! `black_box<T>(value: T) -> T` returns its argument, but the compiler and the C compiler must
//! assume it was read and may have changed, so a benchmark keeps the work it measures. As Rust's,
//! it is a best effort, not a guarantee. It takes any type, which no function written in
//! Sagitario can do for `String`s and classes behind a pointer, so the compiler provides it.
